  "type" : "richtext",
  "display_width" : null,
  "default" : "<p>Segmentation has been a core networking concept for decades. The environments it needs to protect have changed completely.</p><p>SaaS adoption, hybrid workloads, federated identity, and distributed access mean the network edge no longer exists as a defined boundary. Trust is established quickly. Enforcement often is not. The result is exposure that is hard to see and harder to contain.</p><p>When segmentation does not hold, the blast radius of any incident grows. Response takes longer. Recovery costs more. And control — the thing your team is accountable for — is harder to demonstrate.</p>"
